attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a short spine.** Columns 0 to 3, `cusF` to `cusS`, are carried by 93 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0.2 to 94% of calls {S1}. The model names 98 to 99% of them, fewest at column 1, `cusC`, 98% {S1}.

@variable **A single fork and variable stretch runs to the window's end**, columns 4 to 79, carried by 28 to 88%, 51 persistent and 25 shell {S2}. The `fim` genes, columns 8 to 12, are [[fimbria]] {S2.c8-12, Q}. A branch of 5 shell families through columns 17 to 21 runs in 13 to 16%, [[tail]] {S2.b17, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 98 against 90%, and hesitates less there, 0.10 against 0.58 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 6, `ybcH`, a fork column, 1.98 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in the `acr` genes**, columns 77 to 79, `acrA` to `tomB`, carried by 46 to 38% {S2.c77-79}. The last column is `tomB`, in 38% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 90% of genes**, 0.55 bits on average, perplexity 1.7 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.01 against 0.20 bits, and names fewer genes, 82% against 97% {C}.

